WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.280
Deja vu.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.680
In this case, what you don't know can kill you.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:29.300
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.380
I'm Mike.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.520
Hey Mike. Oh, I'm Sean.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.260
And I'm Joe.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.300
Ironically, maybe, deja vu is about amnesia.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.560
Yeah? I think that that's true.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:46.880
I accept this.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.460
Both as a video game and as a term.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.540
Yes. The word means kind.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.720
No, it actually doesn't.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:01.340
It doesn't, right? But experiencing deja vu is a form of amnesia.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.300
It's future amnesia. Yeah.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:06.300
I think we'd be like misrepresenting what deja vu is.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:19.380
But I think if you have amnesia and then you suddenly get like a memory starts coming back to you that you used to have, that would feel like deja vu.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.800
It's like, oh, I feel like this moment's happened before because you're remembering something that happened before.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:28.240
Whereas deja vu, I know, is actually just like something that you're living in right now.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.940
And it feels like you already have that memory.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.180
So they're like adjacent.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:35.480
So it's kind of like, you know, we're not we're not being literal with deja vu.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.160
But yeah, there's still like brain brain not do good work good sometimes.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.240
Exactly.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:48.440
And what deja vu is, is it's a point and click adventure game set in 1941 Chicago.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:02:04.100
You're a private investigator, Ace Harding, who suffers from amnesia, awakes in a bathroom stall and slowly unravels a case that actually involves him.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.860
This is just an NES port.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:18.360
It's not exclusive to the console, but it is kind of in line with some of the other point and click games that we've had on the show.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:25.360
And I guess like the the series of games is known as like Mac Venture style games.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:26.780
These point and click.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.200
Mac Venture. Yeah, I'm not sure.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.740
I don't know enough about the history of these to know why that's called that.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.380
But it's like maybe that's the.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.580
Company or maybe that's.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:36.600
Macintosh adventure games.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.320
