00:52:54.820 --> 00:53:04.260
Having the world explained to you in a way that like, yeah, generally characters that live in a world don't need the world explained to them.

00:53:04.420 --> 00:53:06.360
But maybe somebody with amnesia does.

00:53:06.520 --> 00:53:11.720
And it's a good excuse diegetically to have these explanations made to you.

00:53:12.560 --> 00:53:15.360
Now, that's not so much what's happening here.

00:53:15.360 --> 00:53:20.620
There's no deep lore that's being explained to you as some like outsider to society.

00:53:20.620 --> 00:53:27.180
This is more so just a setup for a mystery that happens to involve you.

00:53:27.380 --> 00:53:32.580
So maybe it's not done for the same reasons, but it's a you know, it's a versatile trope.

00:53:32.660 --> 00:53:34.480
And I think tropes are meant to be used.

00:53:34.640 --> 00:53:38.320
And this is this is a fine use of it.

00:53:38.320 --> 00:53:51.420
And like any good investigator, whether you know it or not at the start of the game, the screen is very similar to Shadowgate in that you have your, you know, your commands or your verbs on the bottom of the screen.

00:53:51.420 --> 00:53:56.460
And then you have your notebook where you're keeping tabs on everything.

00:53:56.640 --> 00:54:00.440
But also, I guess your notebook is your inventory of like things you have.

00:54:00.900 --> 00:54:02.840
And that's on the right hand side of the screen.

00:54:02.840 --> 00:54:13.180
And then on the left hand side is this very small but detailed interactive window of, you know, from your POV, what you're seeing in the scene.

00:54:13.360 --> 00:54:21.800
And you can click on things and you kind of the gameplay loop is you verb into the object.

00:54:22.320 --> 00:54:25.880
And then the game tells you what happens.

00:54:25.880 --> 00:54:27.640
It's very dirty phrasing. Right, right.

00:54:28.140 --> 00:54:29.880
You verb into the noun.

00:54:30.240 --> 00:54:33.740
Right. So, you know, you might search something.

00:54:33.960 --> 00:54:35.260
You might examine something.

00:54:35.460 --> 00:54:37.680
You might open something, take something.

00:54:37.940 --> 00:54:49.000
But this idea of just essentially using that to kind of make the what would have worked as a text adventure game but now with a visual component to it.

00:54:49.460 --> 00:54:58.480
Yeah, yeah. And I'm trying to remember if these because there are some shortcuts in this that make that because what describing like that makes it sound more tedious than it is.

00:54:59.100 --> 00:55:00.860
There are some shortcuts that I can't remember.

00:55:01.000 --> 00:55:07.080
It's still a little tedious. It didn't bother me as much maybe because I wasn't expecting some of these shortcuts.

00:55:07.360 --> 00:55:18.940
Were they in Shadowgate where like you can press B to cancel out of any verb you're doing and then also you can just click on any door, anywhere to move in that direction?

00:55:18.940 --> 00:55:20.640
It's a great question and something.

00:55:20.660 --> 00:55:26.680
It's something I wondered as well because it also like kind of remembers where your cursor was too.

00:55:27.040 --> 00:55:28.920
Right. That's something that I noted.

00:55:29.260 --> 00:55:36.140
Right. If you cancel out of the open thing because you didn't want to open that particular thing, you're still on open rather than having to go back to it.

00:55:36.140 --> 00:55:36.980
Yeah, I guess.

00:55:37.060 --> 00:55:52.880
And the only reason that I said that there is still some tedium is that like no matter how like sort of no matter how intuitive everything else works, you still have to make sure you open doors before you try and walk through.

00:55:54.220 --> 00:55:56.340
True. That'll be something that I kept doing.

00:55:56.620 --> 00:56:00.860
But in general, it's got a good streamline.

00:56:01.360 --> 00:56:09.220
Like, yeah, there's a few pages of items in your inventory pretty quickly that you'll have to like change pages on.

00:56:09.400 --> 00:56:16.740
But in terms of just like at all, you didn't need to read the manual to get how it really worked.

00:56:17.020 --> 00:56:35.640
Right. But if you take it at face value, there are some things that like are obvious that you have to do but could have been shortcuts if they would have made the leaps with the player such as you can't leave a room until you open the door.

00:56:35.640 --> 00:56:39.100
But if you clicked on the move screen, the wherever.

00:56:39.440 --> 00:56:49.240
So there's this other thing on the bottom hand side of the screen where you see move and you have these blue squares which represent any particular area that you can move.

00:56:49.380 --> 00:56:54.060
But it's supposed to be a top down view of the first person view that you're viewing.

00:56:54.320 --> 00:56:59.980
So sometimes this move screen with many squares can get kind of confusing about which square is which.

00:57:00.180 --> 00:57:01.760
Eventually, you'll figure it out in your head.

00:57:01.900 --> 00:57:03.980
But it is a little disorienting at first.

00:57:03.980 --> 00:57:11.680
Just to say I want to move to this door and then the game tell you, you know, you have to open that.

00:57:11.800 --> 00:57:15.760
It's like, okay, but you could have understood that I was trying to do that.

00:57:15.780 --> 00:57:26.860
And it very much does understand that you know that because it's a very, every time that happens, there's a very like talk down to you vibe.

00:57:27.220 --> 00:57:30.860
You can't go through doors before opening them, silly.

00:57:30.860 --> 00:57:32.680
And it's like, okay, thanks.

00:57:32.860 --> 00:57:35.060
Like that should just be assumed.

00:57:35.500 --> 00:57:48.480
And it's important for like things later in the game too that you wouldn't, you know, you wouldn't want certain things to be not necessarily opened, but to examine things, to find things within things.

00:57:48.480 --> 00:57:58.600
You know, that bathroom is like the tutorial where you have to like, sure, there's a coat in front of you and you can just take the coat.

00:57:58.840 --> 00:58:02.880
But if you don't examine it, you won't find out what's inside the coat, you know, and then you have to take those things.

00:58:02.880 --> 00:58:04.380
That actually took me a very long time.

00:58:05.180 --> 00:58:16.260
Right. So it's like, it needs to teach you that right away because otherwise you would just expect that by, you know, by opening something, you automatically get it all.

00:58:16.440 --> 00:58:19.760
Or by examining something, it adds it to your inventory.

00:58:20.020 --> 00:58:21.820
It's like, that's not how it would work.

00:58:21.820 --> 00:58:30.880
Well, I have a question for Joe actually, because I think you kind of gave an acknowledgement of that when I said it.

00:58:31.720 --> 00:58:36.220
How far into this game did you get before you actually went through the pockets of the coat?

00:58:36.880 --> 00:58:40.380
Well, so I was just going to say I had almost the opposite problem.

00:58:41.120 --> 00:58:43.180
I went through the pockets of the coat immediately.

00:58:43.640 --> 00:58:47.440
First thing I did, I examined it, then I went through the pockets, I took everything out of it.

00:58:47.440 --> 00:58:51.700
But then I left, I walked away or whatever, and I was trying to figure out where to go next or whatever.

00:58:51.780 --> 00:58:54.740
And somehow later in the game, I ended up back there.

00:58:55.300 --> 00:58:56.660
And then I took the coat.

00:58:56.900 --> 00:58:59.160
Like I went through the pockets without taking the coat.

00:58:59.540 --> 00:59:02.780
Like I opened the coat while it was still on the hook.

00:59:02.900 --> 00:59:09.780
Wow. And then when you take the coat, underneath the coat is a gun on a holster that was not in the pockets of the coat.

00:59:09.860 --> 00:59:10.880
So it wasn't there.

00:59:10.980 --> 00:59:11.800
So like I did the opposite.

00:59:11.960 --> 00:59:14.640
I was like, oh, intuitively, I think I should open this coat to the side.

00:59:14.640 --> 00:59:19.440
That's really funny. But I didn't take it to see what was underneath it until much later in the game.

00:59:19.520 --> 00:59:21.620
And I was like, oh, I could have used this gun like three times already.

00:59:21.960 --> 00:59:25.680
So I like escaped to the bar.

00:59:26.700 --> 00:59:37.720
I went into the basement through the secret casino and found the dead body and jumped onto the fire escape,

00:59:37.720 --> 00:59:47.260
all while wearing my coat and not knowing that I had money in there, that I had like, that I had clues in there.

00:59:48.140 --> 00:59:52.680
So I got to a point of just like, where the hell am I supposed to get?

00:59:52.940 --> 00:59:55.060
How am I supposed to like acquire currency?

00:59:55.240 --> 00:59:57.460
Like, can I do a day job while I'm out here?

00:59:57.460 --> 01:00:02.920
Like, and then I just, you know, opened the coat and there everything was.

01:00:04.660 --> 01:00:11.440
But I will say there is a, uh, not quite a day job, but I guess it's some people's day job of the casino.

01:00:11.780 --> 01:00:14.060
That is just like an unlimited money creator.

01:00:14.300 --> 01:00:15.780
Well, I needed the money first.

01:00:15.900 --> 01:00:17.260
Did not know that that was the case.

01:00:17.280 --> 01:00:23.900
Yeah, but I think that you can also just, I don't know, but I think you can just like unlimitedly like check the slot machine.

01:00:24.360 --> 01:00:26.500
Like. Oh, wow.

01:00:26.520 --> 01:00:27.480
Find a coin.

01:00:27.860 --> 01:00:29.820
Like one coin or something like that.

01:00:29.820 --> 01:00:31.600
Like, I think there's a way that you're not locked out.

01:00:31.900 --> 01:00:39.640
I just know I want to be at that casino because like, there's never been worse odds for the casino than that specific slot machine.

01:00:39.780 --> 01:00:41.720
Like it, it pays out way too often.

01:00:42.440 --> 01:00:44.700
It's crazy. I didn't even think to gamble.

01:00:45.240 --> 01:00:46.560
And this is me talking.

01:00:46.760 --> 01:00:48.940
Well, I was like, who the hell am I talking to right now?

01:00:49.720 --> 01:00:52.220
Yeah. I ended up with like 30 coins pretty early.

01:00:52.380 --> 01:00:53.220
And then I was like, all right, great.

01:00:53.360 --> 01:00:55.880
I'm like set. Which foreshadowing.

01:00:55.880 --> 01:01:01.500
I just, this is why I got like softlocked three or four times is because I didn't have enough money.

01:01:01.920 --> 01:01:09.100
Not knowing that in addition to not ever being able to spend your $20 bill, did not know that you could gamble.

01:01:09.460 --> 01:01:10.680
So. You can spend it.

01:01:11.920 --> 01:01:12.760
We'll get there.

01:01:13.140 --> 01:01:14.820
Yeah. I think.

01:01:15.000 --> 01:01:16.220
I thought you could. No, you can.

01:01:16.420 --> 01:01:17.520
Yeah. You spend that $20 bill.

01:01:17.660 --> 01:01:20.380
No problem. The cabbie won't take it.

01:01:20.960 --> 01:01:21.760
No. Yeah.

01:01:21.880 --> 01:01:24.380
Nobody takes it. I only know of one place that takes it.

01:01:25.500 --> 01:01:38.200
What I think is so cool about this game is that even when I finally did get stuck and resorted to an FAQ, when I was reading like the order of events, I was like, that's not how I did it.

01:01:38.340 --> 01:01:40.200
Like, did I miss something? But I didn't miss something.

01:01:40.320 --> 01:01:44.320
I just got to the casino probably like less than optimally.

01:01:44.480 --> 01:01:46.380
But there was like another way to get there.

01:01:46.380 --> 01:02:02.100
And it's like, it does give a better sense of a, you know, explore and goof around vibe than Shadowgate was giving where that felt like, yeah, I mean, you know, you could kind of go around, but you were very like locked to the puzzle.

01:02:02.360 --> 01:02:04.720
This isn't like every room is a puzzle.

01:02:04.720 --> 01:02:11.160
This is, you're trying to piece together where to go next based on the information you have.

01:02:11.380 --> 01:02:21.560
Yeah. I did like learning like how there were several entrances and the fact that like, again, you find a key in that jacket that lets you open the front door of the bar.

01:02:21.560 --> 01:02:29.800
And I kept going in thinking that I'm going to have to go up to the third floor of this bar and jump out the window to get back to the street.

01:02:29.940 --> 01:02:36.360
Or I could go down into the sewer and then come up through a hole in the floor to get back into the bar.

01:02:36.480 --> 01:02:38.760
And then I found that there was a key for the front door.

01:02:38.760 --> 01:02:54.760
So yeah, there are several ways to get around the map in addition to several ways to go across like the larger expanse of the game, usually by hailing a cab or just in terms of like order of operations of where you go first.

01:02:55.160 --> 01:02:58.740
Yeah. There's even random events that can happen to you on the street too.

01:02:58.860 --> 01:03:01.340
It's not guaranteed that you're going to be mugged.

01:03:01.840 --> 01:03:06.020
Yeah. But you do get mugged and it is a pain in the ass.

01:03:07.220 --> 01:03:08.860
So what do you do? You just hit that guy, right?

01:03:09.340 --> 01:03:10.660
Yeah, like over and over again.

01:03:11.080 --> 01:03:12.640
Yeah. But I think there's a limit.

01:03:12.780 --> 01:03:17.680
I think if you hit him enough, eventually you will have to pay or he'll hurt you.

01:03:18.040 --> 01:03:20.380
Did you ever get cornered by the lady?

01:03:21.160 --> 01:03:22.280
What's the lady's deal?

01:03:22.360 --> 01:03:23.180
She's got a gun?

01:03:23.680 --> 01:03:24.540
She's got a gun.

01:03:24.880 --> 01:03:29.160
I shot her and then the cops came because I was right in front of the police station.

01:03:29.340 --> 01:03:31.460
Yeah. I'm not proud, but I punched her.

01:03:31.880 --> 01:03:35.240
I think that was the right thing to do actually because she was about to pull a gun on me.

01:03:35.240 --> 01:03:37.160
I was like, I got a puncher.

01:03:37.300 --> 01:03:42.120
Here's the interesting thing and you're getting to what my favorite part of the game is that

01:03:42.120 --> 01:03:46.020
if we think about the Grand Theft Autos or even the L.A.

01:03:46.060 --> 01:03:50.380
Noire of all that stuff, those

01:03:50.380 --> 01:03:55.340
games are so fun not because of the actual story mode, but because of the sandbox environment

01:03:55.340 --> 01:03:58.160
you're put in and how you choose to interact with things.

01:03:58.160 --> 01:04:05.060
And while this game isn't on that scale by any means, there is so much fun that you can

01:04:05.060 --> 01:04:08.540
have in this game by acting like a jackass.

01:04:08.820 --> 01:04:17.200
Oh, yeah. You can get the gun, select shoot, and then self, and the game will be like, oh, wait,

01:04:17.200 --> 01:04:18.300
go out with a bang.

01:04:20.980 --> 01:04:22.540
I did appreciate that.

01:04:22.540 --> 01:04:24.880
I did appreciate that you could shoot whoever you want.

01:04:25.220 --> 01:04:27.460
You would, like, that is the end state.

01:04:27.680 --> 01:04:35.660
I did like that I thought I got around the money thing by starting a car with a key I found,

01:04:35.680 --> 01:04:37.280
and then you immediately just blow up.

01:04:37.640 --> 01:04:43.380
Yeah. And it's not even just like a bullshit, like, wow, how was I supposed to know that?

01:04:43.460 --> 01:04:47.460
Like, if you talk to somebody, or maybe if you read a note or something.

01:04:47.540 --> 01:04:48.520
No, it's the woman.

01:04:48.720 --> 01:04:52.500
Oh, it's the woman. Yeah, she's just like, yeah, yeah, I read that to blow.

01:04:52.720 --> 01:04:53.700
And it's like, oh, okay.

01:04:54.580 --> 01:05:02.980
Yeah. So I do appreciate the level of interaction and all the fun fail states that you got here.

01:05:02.980 --> 01:05:07.840
Yeah. Another fun thing is, like, forget fail states.

01:05:07.980 --> 01:05:11.800
You can also, like, soft lock yourself out of the game by doing really stupid things like

01:05:11.800 --> 01:05:16.680
flushing toilets, flushing your inventory stuff down the toilet.

01:05:16.860 --> 01:05:21.320
Like, literally watching, saying goodbye to the game as you watch it swirl down.

01:05:21.880 --> 01:05:23.400
There's no animation for it, of course.

01:05:23.560 --> 01:05:25.260
The game is kind of lacking that.

01:05:25.420 --> 01:05:28.520
It's all still screens instead of animated screens.

01:05:29.620 --> 01:05:33.420
But then there's also, like, the game is kind of snarky.

01:05:33.540 --> 01:05:34.960
I think you referenced that, Sean.

01:05:35.100 --> 01:05:38.860
But, like, if you're being stupid, it'll imply so.

01:05:39.080 --> 01:05:42.360
But, like, you can use the speak command on that same toilet.

01:05:42.400 --> 01:05:44.920
And the game will tell you, like, you're talking to a toilet.

01:05:45.380 --> 01:05:46.880
Really? I didn't know that.

01:05:47.220 --> 01:05:52.380
Yeah, I didn't either. It's the games that I tried speaking to, and it would just be, like, what are you doing?

01:05:52.600 --> 01:05:57.540
And I thought for a while it was, like, oh, wow, it's actually, maybe it's, if only if

01:05:57.540 --> 01:05:59.240
I talk to that thing it says that.

01:05:59.280 --> 01:06:02.760
But, no. If you talk to inanimate objects, usually it just asks you what you're doing.

01:06:03.680 --> 01:06:08.240
Yeah. Or it says, like, or if you examine them, it says, like, nothing unusual here.

01:06:08.420 --> 01:06:10.880
If you just, like, examine, like, blank spaces or whatever.

01:06:10.880 --> 01:06:15.220
But it is cool that, like, sometimes it does have, like, a little flavor text just to add

01:06:15.220 --> 01:06:17.920
to it. Like, there's a lot to discover in the game.

01:06:18.040 --> 01:06:23.120
Not even just on the way to beating the game, but just exploring the world and seeing what

01:06:23.120 --> 01:06:30.840
you can do. Throughout the game, there are these, I guess we'll call them deja vu moments where there's,

01:06:30.880 --> 01:06:33.760
like, a music cue, and I guess it shows you.

01:06:34.260 --> 01:06:36.660
So now it switches POVs.

01:06:37.320 --> 01:06:38.420
But it shows you.

01:06:38.420 --> 01:06:43.060
And it reveals, like, a, you know, a twist of sorts.

01:06:43.660 --> 01:06:44.920
They get grander.

01:06:45.140 --> 01:06:53.640
But that deja vu moment as a repetitive cue also works really well from a, like, not repetition,

01:06:53.800 --> 01:06:55.240
but even just sound perspective.

01:06:55.560 --> 01:06:56.360
How do you mean?

01:06:56.840 --> 01:07:00.920
Like, just, you know, that, like, every time you hear that specific thing, it's like you've

01:07:00.920 --> 01:07:06.900
learned something bigger than just, like, collecting another thing in your inventory or

01:07:08.160 --> 01:07:08.960
another address.

01:07:09.440 --> 01:07:10.620
Yeah, I guess it was.

01:07:10.740 --> 01:07:17.760
I didn't really put together that whatever was happening would be, like, a big moment.

01:07:17.860 --> 01:07:21.460
Because I remember I was just going up some stairs, and I thought I was just getting, like,

01:07:21.520 --> 01:07:24.740
lightheaded. Because it's like, you don't feel so hot.

01:07:25.740 --> 01:07:28.820
You really need to take a break or something.

01:07:29.000 --> 01:07:30.540
And I'm like, I'm just walking up some stairs.

01:07:30.860 --> 01:07:34.140
And then it didn't happen again until I, like, went to an office.

01:07:34.180 --> 01:07:38.000
And I guess it was my own office.

01:07:38.020 --> 01:07:39.780
But maybe you don't know that yet.

01:07:40.080 --> 01:07:44.260
And you're sort of getting that deja vu, as you might say.

01:07:44.340 --> 01:07:45.520
So, yeah, I guess I see that.

01:07:45.900 --> 01:07:49.240
Yeah. Or, like, when you look at the picture and you recognize yourself.

01:07:49.660 --> 01:07:50.760
That I didn't see.

01:07:50.760 --> 01:07:55.380
Oh, yeah. There's, like, a picture on the wall that is of Bob Oxer.

01:07:55.560 --> 01:07:59.320
It's you. And then that image comes up of your face, and that music plays.

01:07:59.540 --> 01:08:02.840
And it's a little corny, but it is kind of, like, it is kind of cool.

01:08:03.000 --> 01:08:04.240
And it's kind of, like, mysterious.

01:08:04.240 --> 01:08:08.240
And it catches your interest of, like, oh, man, what is going on?

01:08:08.320 --> 01:08:10.460
Like, this is such a creepy situation for this guy to be in.

01:08:10.560 --> 01:08:13.360
You got to just kind of suspend your, like, cringe a little bit.

01:08:13.780 --> 01:08:17.840
And while you guys were talking about whether or not you pulled the items out of the coat,

01:08:17.860 --> 01:08:19.960
the first moment where I...

01:08:20.760 --> 01:08:26.040
I had to actually look at a guide was because the desk in the...

01:08:26.040 --> 01:08:28.780
Above the bar in the office didn't...

01:08:28.780 --> 01:08:29.700
You weren't...

01:08:29.700 --> 01:08:32.040
Because of the point of view, you're facing...

01:08:32.040 --> 01:08:33.500
It didn't read like a desk, did it?

01:08:33.680 --> 01:08:36.380
It didn't... I mean, like, the guy was hunched over it, if I recall.

01:08:36.520 --> 01:08:38.220
Like, there was another one that wasn't.

01:08:38.340 --> 01:08:40.540
But there was another one where a guy's hunched over the desk.

01:08:40.540 --> 01:08:41.480
So, you knew it was a desk.

01:08:41.700 --> 01:08:44.220
But he... The drawers would be on his side.

01:08:44.400 --> 01:08:45.980
So, you would think you have to, like... Yeah, you can't see there's anything to open.

01:08:46.220 --> 01:08:49.760
Right, right. But the only way to progress is to open those drawers.

01:08:50.160 --> 01:08:54.300
And so, I guess I could have just tried spamming commands around the room.

01:08:54.460 --> 01:08:55.940
But I don't have time for that.

01:08:56.140 --> 01:08:57.060
So, that was...

01:08:57.060 --> 01:08:58.260
Yeah, it kind of defeats the purpose of the game.

01:08:58.360 --> 01:08:59.580
You're not even playing the game anymore.

01:08:59.700 --> 01:09:00.540
You're just... I got there.

01:09:00.760 --> 01:09:03.660
That's like, you know, maybe you guys knew you could gamble.

01:09:04.060 --> 01:09:06.240
At least I opened that...

01:09:06.240 --> 01:09:08.720
I opened that desk pretty easily.

01:09:10.200 --> 01:09:11.740
Yeah, I did the same thing as Mike.

01:09:11.840 --> 01:09:13.800
I was like... I had no idea.

